// AVIF - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// AVIF, HEIF and a JPEG XL container are all ISO base media file
// format: a flat list of boxes, each a 4-byte size, a 4-byte type,
// and that many bytes.
//
// The quirk is that the size includes the header, so a reader has to
// read the type before it can decide whether a 64-bit size follows.
//
// The greeting goes in a `free` box, which is the format's own skip
// space -- the same role as a PNG tEXt chunk and a GIF comment
// extension, expressed as a box.
//
// Hello World! is in that box. The rest of this file is not a
// playable image and does not claim to be.
//
// avif: 44 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 00 00 00 18 66 74 79 70 61 76 69 66 00 00 00 00 |....ftypavif....|   <- 0000
// 61 76 69 66 6D 69 66 31 00 00 00 14 66 72 65 65 |avifmif1....free|   <- 0010
// 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21             |Hello World!|   <- 0020
